    "text": "A square is inscribed in the circle $x^2+y^2-10 x-6 y+30=0$. One side of this square is parallel to $y=x+3$. If $\\left(x_i, y_i\\right)$ are the vertices of the square, then $\\mathbf{\\Sigma}\\left(x_i^2+y_i^2\\right)$ is equal to:",
